* MOSFET Boost — exported from Lutherie
* One small MOSFET in common source. Gain sets how much of the source resistor is bypassed, from about 4 dB to over 30 dB. The very high input impedance keeps the guitar's treble, and when pushed it clips softly and unevenly, a little like a tube.

Vsig SIGSRC 0 SIN(0 0.3 220.0) AC 1
Rsig SIGSRC IN 1k
CC1 IN N2 47n
RR1 VCC_9V N2 1Meg
RR2 N2 0 1Meg
MM1 N4 N2 N5 N5 M_2N7000
CM1gs N2 N5 20p
CM1gd N2 N4 5p
RR3 VCC_9V N4 2.7k
RR4 N5 0 2.2k
CC3 N5 N6 47u
* Gain pot 5k B taper at 50%
RVR1a 0 0 2.5k
RVR1b 0 N6 2.5k
CC2 N4 OUT 4.7u
RR5 OUT 0 100k
Rload OUT 0 1Meg
VVS1 VCC_9V_src 0 DC 9.0
RVS1s VCC_9V_src VCC_9V 0.01

.model M_2N7000 NMOS(Level=1 Vto=2.0 Kp=0.12 Lambda=0.0003 Is=1e-13)

.options reltol=1e-5 abstol=1e-13 vntol=1e-8 method=trap
.tran 1.3020833333333333e-06 0.3 0 1.3020833333333333e-06
.control
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=12
run
wrdata mosfet_boost.ngspice.txt v(OUT)
.endc
.end